 <26456472+HachebeDLC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:54:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v1.2.2 rebase: register Hades II 1.0.141667, the two-call
 GMalloc test, new switches documented
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hades II's patches.py names the 1.0.141667 update's main (a862861f…), which the
profile now registers as a build (test_patches checks every named build). The
ue_malloc finder returns its calls as a list and accepts the two close
setups of DRAGON BALL Sparking! ZERO, so its tests expect that; three calls
stay red. docs/env_switches.tsv gets meanings for the switches the iOS ports
read, and docs/agents/game-patches.md is regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DdPiRBdo6BGoU2TSvWZ4sW

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: keeps the iOS ports (patches 0084-0090) consistent with the v1.2.2 engine: the Hades II build our patches name, the ue_malloc two-call rule, the switches they read
Issue: HachebeDLC/NX2Apple#1

---
 dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv |  1 +
 dm/tools/tests/test_ue_malloc.py   | 14 +++++++++-----
 docs/env_switches.tsv              | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv b/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
index 30b9784b..55203030 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
+++ b/dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ pad_layout	full
 # The update's build IDs come from its own ExeFS (the base game's from upstream's profile).
 build	v0	0.0.126424	main=5219053e5eb156be80fbb2f303779531	sdk=d83a56a5558798414c78ec722867a7da
 build	v1	1.0.137848	main=8ce1ac48e9fa74479051f3520e632df4	sdk=190030518b5d64e5d87b84bc54661af9
+build	v655360	1.0.141667	main=a862861fa2eeedea1d873c94324fca7b	sdk=190030518b5d64e5d87b84bc54661af9
 package	v1
 shader_versions	v0 v1
 
diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_ue_malloc.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_ue_malloc.py
index 0bc3d8d4..cfd411cd 100644
--- a/dm/tools/tests/test_ue_malloc.py
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_ue_malloc.py
@@ -45,11 +45,11 @@ def find(img): return ue_malloc.find(bytes(img), TEXT, RO, DATA)
 class FindTest(unittest.TestCase):
     def test_found_in_place(self):
         call, vt, slot, why = find(image())
-        self.assertEqual((call, vt, slot), (CALLER + 4, VT, 19), why)
+        self.assertEqual((call, vt, slot), ([CALLER + 4], VT, 19), why)
 
     def test_found_through_relocations(self):
         call, vt, slot, why = find(image(slot=26, relocated=True))
-        self.assertEqual((call, vt, slot), (CALLER + 4, VT, 26), why)
+        self.assertEqual((call, vt, slot), ([CALLER + 4], VT, 26), why)
 
     def test_no_name_is_not_red(self):
         call, _, _, why = find(image(name=False))
@@ -61,10 +61,14 @@ class FindTest(unittest.TestCase):
         self.assertIsNone(call)
         self.assertTrue(why.startswith('[RED] ') and 'slot 20' in why, why)
 
-    def test_two_calls_are_red(self):
-        call, _, _, why = find(image(calls=2))
+    def test_two_close_calls_are_the_duplicated_setup(self):   # DRAGON BALL Sparking! ZERO sets GMalloc up twice, 0x518 bytes apart: both calls are cut
+        call, vt, slot, why = find(image(calls=2))
+        self.assertEqual((call, vt, slot), ([CALLER + 4, CALLER + 12], VT, 19), why)
+
+    def test_three_calls_are_red(self):
+        call, _, _, why = find(image(calls=3))
         self.assertIsNone(call)
-        self.assertTrue(why.startswith('[RED] ') and '2 calls' in why, why)
+        self.assertTrue(why.startswith('[RED] ') and '3 calls' in why, why)
 
 
 if __name__ == '__main__':
diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 3f37f7b1..b6d42d25 100644
